{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487579696,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk2ODgwOTkxNQ=="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487579696,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk2ODgwOTkxNw=="},"added":["annex"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487579696,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk2ODgwOTkxOA=="},"added":["performance"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1487615281,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MTE1MDc2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1314#issuecomment-281150765"},"message":"Benjamin Poldrack wrote:\n\u003e A call to either git status or git annex status can be very expensive in large\n\u003e submodule hierarchies. For git status there's --ignore-submodules, which can be\n\u003e used to examine just the repository we are in without inspecting its\n\u003e submodules. Since this is way faster while it often provides all we actually\n\u003e need, I'd love to see that option for git annex status, too.\n\u003e Any chance to get this, @joeyh ?\n\u003e \n\u003e In a way, this might be related to how to fix http://git-annex.branchable.com/\n\u003e bugs/git_annex_status_fails_with_submodule_in_direct_mode/\n\nI can't make git-annex status -- --ignore-submodules pass the option\nthrough to git status, because the current interface treats that as\ngetting the status of a file with a name that happens to start with a\ndash, so git-annex changes it to ./--ignore-submodules when passing it\nto git status.\n\nSo, this would have to be a switch added to git-annex status. There\ndon't seem to be many other switches that it would make sense to need to\npass through either. Perhaps --ignored ?\n\nBut first, I wonder if passing specific files/dirs to git-annex status\nand avoiding the submodule could avoid the cost. That could be hard or\neasy depending on what you're doing, I suppose.\n\nAlso of course, there's no need to use git-annex status instead of git\nstatus itself, unless the repo is direct mode or you're using its --json\nfeature.\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487616844,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MTE1NjcyNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1314#issuecomment-281156725"},"message":"\u003e Perhaps --ignored ?\n\nIn general I'm fine with any switch as long as it works. ;-) But I think the name should contain some notion of submodules. May be `--no-subs` if it is about length.\n\n\u003e But first, I wonder if passing specific files/dirs to git-annex status\nand avoiding the submodule could avoid the cost.\n\nTechnically yes. But if I need to know the status of the superproject, that approach would mean to list all files plus the dirs, that are no submodules. I can't just pass `.`. So this would basically simply be datalad to implement that feature instead of annex. But we can do that of course. I just think, it would be a reasonable thing to have in annex as well.\n\n\u003e there's no need to use git-annex status instead of git\nstatus itself, unless the repo is direct mode or you're using its --json\nfeature.\n\nRight, I'm aware. But I do use the --json feature and furthermore I'd rather like to rely on annex than make the distinction on our own. It's just safer and more reliable for us to let annex decide what to do in the current mode or version of an annex repository, I think. Otherwise we tend to ignore, that there's more than just v5 indirect mode. ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"625d4f81fd78f1510c65762d99779f95c491087f"},"timestamp":1487624561,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MTE4MDYxNg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1314#issuecomment-281180616"},"message":"Implemented git-annex status --ignore-submodules=when\n\n-- \nsee shy jo","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487658126,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MTI1NTc5Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1314#issuecomment-281255796"},"message":"Thank you, @joeyh !","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487658126,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50OTcwMTc2NDEz"},"status":2}]}